":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"State-changing actions had clear roles: installing repository tooling, creating repository content and configuration, enabling the hardened service and firewall access, disabling remote repositories, installing the target package, completing the mandatory reboot protocol, and cleaning caches. One unnecessary bounded mutation occurred: cmd-016c93f587304f61 attempted an already-installed jq package and refreshed local metadata, so it did not provide the intended negative-control evidence; package state was unchanged and cache residue was subsequently removed by cmd-962d3493c8fd4439 and cmd-9272bf966e484963. No failed services, damaged package state, abandoned reboot unit, or unexplained temporary residue remained. The restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot ID, recovered services/data, and lifecycle cross-checks all agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-016c93f587304f61","cmd-d7455c7e19544fe6","cmd-48a3d919e8684475","cmd-47cafc78ba6b4bd2","cmd-bce83fdab76b4146","cmd-9272bf966e484963","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 serves a functional local repository, tree was installed through it with the usual remote repositories disabled, and the RHEL release and kernel were preserved. The mandatory node-restart protocol was directly and coherently demonstrated.","limitations":["Remote unavailability during installation was demonstrated at the DNF configuration and resolution level by disabling BaseOS/AppStream and failing to resolve a remote-only package; no transport-layer network outage was captured at that exact time."]}
